<title>GREECE: GREEK RETAIL SALES RISE 7.2PCT YR/YR IN SEPTEMBER.</title>
<headline>GREEK RETAIL SALES RISE 7.2PCT YR/YR IN SEPTEMBER.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's retail sales (turnover) rose 7.2 percent year-on-year in September from 10.2 percent in August, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Foodstuffs rose 2.5 percent, apparel and footwear by 0.6</p>
<p>percent, furniture and household goods by 7.5 percent and</p>
<p>miscellaneous by 18 percent, NSS said.</p>
<p>Average sales were up 10.4 percent year-on-year in the</p>
<p>period January-September, it said.</p>
<p>    Retail sales	  Sept 96     Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year(pct)	7.2	 10.2	  9.5</p>
<p>    Index (1988=100)     254.7	230.4	237.6</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
